+## 4. UI + interaction
+
+`D7_D8_UI_CHANGE_LIMITED`. The application gains no component, state, route, feature, token, or motion. The only product changes are the D7 corrections plus the D8 coherent Scanner-card link semantics, named Ticker/Positions contrast and sparkline semantics, auth-dialog opener restoration, and focus-scroll reachability for three existing controls at proven page scale 2 described below. The separate 393×852 composition does not change. Everything else in this section defines the maintainer-facing command/report interaction and the existing application states the gates observe.
+
+**Flows:**
+
+The command hierarchy is fixed:
+
+| Operator intent | Nx target | npm command | Behavior |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Retain full existing Chromium suite | `dashboard-e2e:e2e` | `npm run browser:chromium` | Run exactly the checked 52-test pre-feature Chromium inventory. |
+| Check bounded engine matrix | `dashboard-e2e:compat` | `npm run browser:compat` | Run only the five named journeys in Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit. |
+| Check automated accessibility | `dashboard-e2e:a11y` | `npm run browser:a11y` | Run the nine axe scans plus named real-browser semantic/keyboard assertions. |
+| Compare approved screenshots | `dashboard-e2e:visual` | `npm run browser:visual` | Compare only; missing or changed baselines fail. |
+| Write candidate screenshots deliberately | `dashboard-e2e:visual-update` | `npm run browser:visual:update -- --authorization {receipt_path}` | Validate the durable authorization, write only current-platform candidates, and emit the candidate-set receipt; never approve. |
+| Run merge floor | `dashboard-e2e:quality` | `npm run browser:quality` | Invoke Chromium, compatibility, accessibility, and visual checks once each; never update. |
+
+`npm run ci` and the hosted workflow may depend on the aggregate check but have no path to `browser:visual:update`.
+
+The closed five-journey compatibility inventory is:
+
+1. Public Landing → Ticker client-side navigation, browser Back/Forward, and route-parameter binding.
+2. Deterministic content-full Ticker, then isolated stream loss with static content retained and live-derived content visibly degraded.
+3. Signed-out protected-route wall, then sign-in dialog keyboard entry, close, and return focus.
+4. Signed-in dense Positions at 393px with keyboard-reachable expansion/collapse and route navigation.
+5. Signed-in dense Scanner at table and mobile-card widths with its deterministic degraded state and route navigation.
+
+Settings belongs to accessibility coverage, not a sixth compatibility journey. Each journey has a state-specific readiness/vacuity guard and runs once in each pinned engine.
