+The visual acceptance flow is two-stage and receipt-bound. After a failed compare, an `owner` or `design_reviewer` inspects expected/actual/diff and authors the exact durable `visual-review/authorizations/{authorization_id}.json` receipt from §2. The update command verifies that receipt, writes candidate bytes, and emits only `candidate-sets/{candidate_set_id}.json` with their hashes. A `code_reviewer` then authors `acceptances/{candidate_set_id}.json` to accept or reject those exact PNG/source-diff hashes. The command cannot author either human decision and never transitions beyond `candidates_written`. Accepted bytes become merge-eligible only after two independent clean compare-only runs establish `stability_clean`. Linux follows the manual protected candidate workflow and reviewed commit/bootstrap path in §2; push/PR/aggregate/check workflows remain compare-only.
